              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi fb
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{fb}{\to} \Sigma
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian+density"} local Lagrangian density
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            %em local BV-BRST complex
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %em local BRST complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            not on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi Σ
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \tau_{\Sigma} \alpha
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functionals"} functionals
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi EL
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{\Sigma}(E)_{\delta_{EL} = 0}
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgressions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\Sigma}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+differential+forms"} variational differential forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \Omega^{\bullet, \bullet}_\Sigma(E)
            on the jet bundle, but on these variational differential forms themselves (whence “local”, i.e. before
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+differential"} BV-BRST differential
            in a BV-resolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi BV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\bullet,\bullet}_\Sigma(E)\vert_{\mathcal{E}_{BV}}
            of the restriction to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ↪
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} \hookrightarrow J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\bullet,\bullet}_\Sigma(E)
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+spacetime+derivative"} total spacetime derivative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            (horizontal derivative), then the
            %em local BV-BRST cohomology
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s + d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
          %p
            Generally, considering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+differential+forms"} variational differential forms
            up to
            = succeed "-exact" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration
            involved in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+by+parts"} integration by parts
            and it is in this way that “local BV-BRST cohomology” knows about the actual BV-BRST cohomology on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
          %h2#example Example
          %p
            Consider local coordinates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi^a)
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antifield"} antifield
            coordinates are to be denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\phi}_a
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+differential"} BV-BRST differential
            takes them to the corresponding component
