          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\epsilon^\alpha)
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antighosts"} antighosts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi c
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{c}_\alpha
            are taken by the BV-BRST differential to the antifield-preimage of the term on the left:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi c
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi α
                    %mo )
